my/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-164333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.99,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.99\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.3263.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99)=2.3263.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-164333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5788a43d39efd18f8569ede86ccb8514d5f74b2c33530e746849caf8e813c650"} {"question" "q-164333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-164333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1.2816"] ["math" "-2.3263"] ["math" "1.2816"] ["math" "2.3263"] ["math" "3.0902"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-164333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.3263"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.001.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 3.0902)=0.999.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 3.0902)=1-0.999=0.001.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-3.0902)=0.001.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/assets/12d4d863466f8a7c1ff72d5c08fed94097ac23d94e04a2976603a3f3a78f6261.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-3.0902) & =0.001 \\\\ P(Z\\le -3.0902) & =0.001.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-3.0902.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5788a43d39efd18f8569ede86ccb8514d5f74b2c33530e746849caf8e813c650"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1.9600"] ["math" "-2.5758"] ["math" "-3.0902"] ["math" "2.3263"] ["math" "3.0902"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "q-96954" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3.0902"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/state.json" "file_sha256" "7e082324addbb527d625ee03ef823a1467f051401aca243ea9d229e975440f35"} {"question" "e-8526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070279/example-8526.json" "file_sha256" "28aa9cf5f1b0f57b310e2319a5c0d